{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall appoint Elazar.</b> For he is appointed over them to carry them — the oil, the incense, and the anointing oil — <b>and the daily meal-offering</b> — upon him it is placed to command and to urge and to offer it at the time of their encampment (Jerusalem Talmud Shabbat 10)." "<b>You shall appoint all the Tabernacle.</b> And further, he was appointed over the burden of the sons of Kehat — to assign each man to his service and to his burden. And that is <b>the Tabernacle and all that is in it</b> — all the arrangements detailed above in this passage. But the burden of the sons of Gershon and Merari, which is not of the Holy of Holies, was under Itamar, as written in the passage of Naso."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:23.097420218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}